==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|ль}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*li}}. Shortened variant {{m|ru|ль}} is attested since 14th century.<ref>{{R:ru:Vasmer|ли, ль|491|2}}</ref><ref>{{cite-book|title=Лекціи по исторіи русскаго языка|author=А. И. Соболевскій|authorlink=ru:Соболевский, Алексей Иванович|page=96|year=1907|publisher=Университетская типографія|location=Москва|edition=4th|url=https://archive.org/details/sobolevsky-a-i-lektsii-po-istorii-russkogo-yazyka-1907/page/96/}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-ли.ogg}}

===Particle===
{{head|ru|particle}}

# {{lb|ru|interrogative particle|placed after the first word in a sentence or phrase}} Do/does/did...? Is/are/was/were...?
#: {{uxi|ru|[[знать|Зна́ете]] '''ли''' [[вы́]]?|'''Do''' you know?}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[хорошо|Хорошо́]] '''ли''' [[ему|ему́]]?|'''Is''' he okay?}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[отправить|Отпра́вил]] '''ли''' [[я́]] [[письмо́]]?|'''Did''' I send the letter?}}

===Conjunction===
{{head|ru|conjunction}}

# [[whether]], [[if]]

====Usage notes====
* The subordinate clause with '''ли''' expresses an occurrence (i.e., an event, incident, news, or rumor) that happened in the past or that could possibly happen in the future. In this specific case, the main clause shows confirming or denying the occurrence (as described in the subordinate clause with '''ли'''). For example:
:* {{uxi|ru|Они спросят, '''отдыхал ли Андрей раньше'''.|They will ask '''if Andrei has been on a holiday before'''.}}
:: (The subordinate clause is an occurrence that happened in the past.)
:* {{uxi|ru|Он не скажет, '''останется ли он дома'''.|He will not say '''if he will stay home'''.}}
:: (The subject of the main clause and the subordinate clause denotes the same person "he". The subordinate clause is an occurrence that could possibly happen in the future.)
: The main clause often has a verb that describes an occurrence, such as verbs pertaining to asking or talking. And also, depending on the context, the subordinate clause with '''ли''' could be regarded as indirect speech.
* To make a sentence that expresses curiosity about a topic while using '''ли''' in the subordinate clause, '''{{m|ru|интере́сно}}, ....''' is often used for the main clause. For example:
:* {{uxi|ru|'''(Мне) интересно,''' будет ли она на тусовке.|('''(I) am interested (wonder)''' if she will be at the party.}}
:* {{uxi|ru|Я вызвала такси, вышла, нашла - а её чуть не увели! Представляешь, уже стоит парень и '''интересуется не его ли такси''' я говорю - моя машинка!|I called a taxi, went outside, found it and my ride was almost stolen! Guess what, a guy had already been there and '''wondering if''' that was his cab. I said "that's my cab!"}}
* To make a sentence that expresses doubt about a topic while using '''ли''' in the subordinate clause, '''(SUB) {{m|ru|[[не]] [[знать]]}}, ....''', '''(SUB) {{m|ru|не [[помнить]]}}, ....''', '''(SUB) {{m|ru|сомнева́ться}}, ....''', and '''{{m|ru|[[трудно|Тру́дно]] [[сказа́ть]]}}, ....''' are often used for the main clause. For example:
:* {{uxi|ru|'''Я не знаю,''' говорит ли мой дедушка по-арабски.|'''I don't know''' if my grandfather speaks Arabic.}}
:: (The main clause shows a doubtful attitude by not knowing whether the old man speaks Arabic.)
:* {{uxi|ru|'''Я не помню,''' выключил ли я телевизор.|'''I don't remember''' if I turned off the television.}}
:: (The main clause shows a doubtful attitude by not remembering whether the television is turned off.)
:* {{uxi|ru|'''Я сомневаюсь,''' курил ли я сигареты часто.|'''I doubt''' that I smoked cigarettes often.}}
:: (The main clause shows a doubtful attitude by being skeptical about the smoking habit in the past.)
:* {{uxi|ru|'''Трудно сказать,''' поймут ли волонтёры установки этого задания.|'''It's difficult to tell''' that the volunteers understand the guidelines of this task.}}
:: (The main clause shows a doubtful attitude by having a difficulty of explaining about the volunteers' situation.)

